The Chulapa theme uses specific HTML tags for the "Related posts" section. According to the [Layouts documentation](https://dieghernan.github.io/chulapa/docs/04-layouts#recommendations), the heading for this panel is hardcoded as an `<h2>` with the Bootstrap class `h5`.

To keep the text small without changing the heading level, you should use custom CSS in your `assets/css/custom.scss` file. This allows you to adjust the visual appearance while preserving the semantic structure.

```scss
/* In assets/css/custom.scss */
h2.h5 {
  /* Your custom styling to keep text small */
  font-size: 1rem; 
}
```

Note that the theme's structure for related/random panels is handled by internal renderers. For more details on layout components, see [Layout structure and components](https://dieghernan.github.io/chulapa/docs/04-layouts#layout-structure-and-components).

After editing your CSS, restart your local Jekyll server to see the changes.
